{
  "__RATINGS_ARE_ESTIMATES": "IMPORTANT. The 29 sub-stat ratings in this file are ESTIMATES, calibrated by hand against public tournament results. They are not measured data and no such data exists. Only the following fields are factual: pr, pr_rank, org, region, age band, and the tournament record described in each note. Everything else is one person's read of how these players play, written to make the simulation behave sensibly.",
  "__DATA_SNAPSHOT": "Epic Power Rankings, August 2026.",
  "__PRIVACY_RULES": "Players are keyed by GAMERTAG - that is their competitive identity. `real_name` appears ONLY where the player is an adult and the name is publicly documented. Under-18 players have NO name and NO birthdate, only an age. No player in this file is given an `ego` or any other personality-defect rating; those are for generated fictional players only.",
  "__PEAK": "Only `peak_overall` is authored here. The engine derives a per-sub-stat ceiling from it (see realPlayers.ts -> derivePeak), so the peak of each individual sub-stat is a consequence of the design, not another number to maintain. Peak is hidden in the UI by exactly the same rule as every other player.",

  "settings": {
    "__doc": "How the real reference players behave as signings. They are all under contract at their real orgs, so prising one loose costs a buyout on top of their wage. Tune these to make the top of the scene more or less reachable.",
    "salaryMultiplier": 1.0,
    "__salaryMultiplier": "Applied on top of the normal salary curve in balance.json. These are the 12 best players alive, so the curve already makes them expensive.",
    "buyoutMultiplier": { "min": 26, "max": 44 },
    "__buyoutMultiplier": "Buyout = weekly salary * this. Much steeper than the 8-20 a generated player asks, because none of these orgs want to sell. Lower it if you want a superteam to be achievable early.",
    "contractWeeks": { "min": 30, "max": 78 },
    "minReputationToSign": 42,
    "__minReputationToSign": "Your org must be at least this famous before a top-12 player will take the call at all. Set to 0 to let a week-1 nobody sign the world champion.",
    "minTierEntered": 2,
    "__minTierEntered": "The real orgs only bother entering events of this tier or above. Tier 1 is the Open Practice Cup - the best duos in the world are not playing that, so you get the lower rungs of the ladder to yourself.",
    "internationalFromTier": 5,
    "__internationalFromTier": "At this tier and above the event is treated as INTERNATIONAL: every real org enters regardless of region, so the FNCS Grand Finals puts you in a lobby with Falcons and BIG at the same time. Below it you only meet the orgs based in your own region.",
    "scoutLevelAtStart": 2,
    "__scoutLevelAtStart": "These players are public figures - everyone already knows roughly how good they are, so they start partly scouted instead of totally unknown."
  },

